{
  "id": "dynamic-skill-theory",
  "term": "dynamic skill theory",
  "definition": "Dynamic skill theory is a theory of cognitive development that views skills in action and thought, including speech and gestures, as developing through hierarchically ordered levels. Higher-level abilities are built by combining lower-level skills across sensorimotor, representational, and abstract tiers, and this growth is not simply linear.",
